course: dictionary
lesson: 8255
title: Ribwort: a wild plant in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A ribwort is a common wild plant. You can find it on lawns and by roads. Its name tells you a clue: «rib» means a strong line, like the ribs inside your body, and ribwort leaves have strong lines like that.
explain: The sentence gives you more clues. «Ribwort plantain stems can be looped to flick their heads like little guns.» Stems and heads tell you it is a plant. The word «flick» tells you the heads come off easily when you hit them.
explain: Look for small words that show a change of idea. In «in Ukraine people put plantain leaves on cuts, but a cut is best cleaned with water and covered with a plaster», the word «but» shows the sentence is changing direction. The second part gives the safe advice: clean a cut with water and cover it.
fact: Ribwort is a noun. It is the name of a thing, here a plant.
fact: «Ribwort» means a common wild plant with long narrow leaves that have strong lines, and a dark brown flower head on a tall stalk.
fact: «Ribwort plantain» is the full name you will see in books and on nature walks.
fact: Children in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand play a game called «soldiers» or «conkers with plantains», flicking the heads off each other's stalks.
fact: Ribwort is often found growing on lawns and roadsides, so it is easy to spot on a walk.
exercise: «Ribwort plantain stems can be looped to flick their heads like little guns.» What is ribwort? | *A common wild plant with long leaves that have strong lines | A type of castle | A sweet from the shop | A kind of plaster for cuts
exercise: Which clue in the sentence tells you ribwort is a plant with stalks? | little | looped | guns | *stems
exercise: What do the «ribs» in ribwort remind you of? | The wings of a bird | The stones of a castle | The water in a pond | *The strong lines on the leaves
test: «In Ukraine people put plantain leaves on cuts, but a cut is best cleaned with water and covered with a plaster.» Which small word shows that the sentence changes direction? | cuts | *but | people | in
test: Children in Australia play «soldiers» with ribwort. What is the game about? | Catching a ball | *Flicking the heads off each other's stalks | Building sandcastles | Counting the leaves on a lawn
exam: Ella reads «ribwort plantain» and does not know it. What should she do first? | Guess it is a kind of car | *Read the words around it, then check a dictionary if she is still unsure | Skip the whole lesson forever | Give up and never read the text again
